From b6ecd62398d98f10ab2432816182f777b784ef6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:31:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Kernels: review (dead check, documentation, saturated
 micromorphic damage)

- The check of the finite element of the cached values of the shape
  functions could never fail (the cache belongs to the finite element):
  removed. Only a different number of points reveals a destroyed rule.
- The documentation of GradientsComputation lists all the supported
  behaviours and no longer names the quadrature interpolator of MFEM.
- The comment of the tests on the debug device states that, without
  device, the stiffness matrices are computed by the version for the host,
  the kernel being then only run by the variants on the GPU in the Debug
  and Coverage builds.
- MicromorphicKernelsTest imposes a micromorphic damage up to 2.5, so that
  the damage is bounded by one near the boundary (a value greater than 2
  is required with the material properties of the test), and checks it,
  on all the processes.
---
 ...nearEvolutionProblemImplementationBase.hxx | 19 +++++++-----
 src/Batch/ElementsGeometry.cxx                |  3 +-
 src/Batch/Gradients.cxx                       |  3 +-
 tests/CMakeLists.txt                          |  9 ++++--
 tests/MicromorphicKernelsTest.cxx             | 31 ++++++++++++++-----
 5 files changed, 43 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/MFEMMGIS/NonLinearEvolutionProblemImplementationBase.hxx b/include/MFEMMGIS/NonLinearEvolutionProblemImplementationBase.hxx
index c696f5f88c..f0b1e571df 100644
--- a/include/MFEMMGIS/NonLinearEvolutionProblemImplementationBase.hxx
+++ b/include/MFEMMGIS/NonLinearEvolutionProblemImplementationBase.hxx
@@ -80,14 +80,17 @@ namespace mfem_mgis {
      * \brief name of the parameter selecting the computation of the
      * gradients in the integration by batches: `ElementByElement` (default:
      * the behaviour integrators compute the gradients element by element)
-     * or `Kernels` (the derivatives of the unknowns are computed for all the
-     * elements by the quadrature interpolator of MFEM, then each behaviour
-     * integrator computes its gradients by a kernel, on the device if a
-     * device is enabled). `Kernels` requires `BehaviourIntegration` set to
-     * `Batch`, and is supported for the standard mechanical behaviours in
-     * 3D, plane strain and plane stress, without FBar, on meshes with one
-     * geometry. The default value is given by the environment variable
-     * `MFEM_MGIS_GRADIENTS_COMPUTATION`, if defined.
+     * or `Kernels` (the derivatives and, if required, the values of the
+     * unknowns are computed for all the elements by a kernel, then each
+     * behaviour integrator computes its gradients by a kernel, on the device
+     * if a device is enabled). `Kernels` requires `BehaviourIntegration` set
+     * to `Batch`, and is supported, in 3D, plane strain and plane stress,
+     * for the standard mechanical behaviours (small and finite strain,
+     * without FBar nor regularisation), the stationary non linear heat
+     * transfer behaviours, the transient term of the heat equation and the
+     * micromorphic damage behaviours, on meshes with one geometry (NURBS
+     * meshes excepted). The default value is given by the environment
+     * variable `MFEM_MGIS_GRADIENTS_COMPUTATION`, if defined.
      */
     static const char* const GradientsComputation;
     /*!
